# Carunel website — example environment configuration
#
# FORMSPREE_FORM_ID
# ------------------
# Public Formspree form ID for the Contact page inquiry form.
# Get one by creating a form at https://formspree.io. It is a public
# identifier, not a secret — Formspree form IDs are meant to be embedded
# in client-side code (see js/config.js).
#
# For the GitHub Pages deploy (.github/workflows/pages.yml), set this as
# a repository VARIABLE (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions >
# Variables), not a secret — see README.md for the exact steps. The
# workflow passes it to `npm run build`, which injects it into
# dist/js/config.js.
#
# For local verification, build with:
#   FORMSPREE_FORM_ID=your-form-id npm run build
#
# For everyday local editing, this site still needs no build step at
# all — a plain static file server works. To try the inquiry form
# locally without running the build, copy the value directly into
# js/config.js instead:
#
#   window.CARUNEL_CONFIG = { FORMSPREE_FORM_ID: 'your-form-id' };
#
# Leaving this unset keeps the inquiry form hidden; the "Email Carunel
# Directly" option on the Contact page remains visible either way.
FORMSPREE_FORM_ID=
